## Cursor-agent integration (`automation/` package)
Uses the Cursor SDK (`cursor-sdk`). Reads the key from env `CURSOR_API_KEY` (NEVER stored in
repo); optional model override `CURSOR_MODEL` (default `auto`). Files:
- `automation/_common.py` — key/model loading, `run_one_shot()` (one-shot `Agent.prompt`,
  splits startup vs run failures), path constants.
- `automation/self_heal.py` — **primary use case.** On a workflow failure, launches a Cursor
  agent against the project to diagnose (and with `--apply`, fix) the failing script/node.
  Diagnose-only by default; writes a report to `automation/heal_reports/heal-<ts>.md`.
  CLI: `--node`, `--message`, `--stdin` (JSON error object), `--apply`.
- `automation/generate_script.py` — OPTIONAL/off-label: generate a video script via a Cursor
  agent as an A/B alternative to the Groq node. Prints the same JSON contract
  (title/description/sections/script) to stdout. Groq remains the default.
NOTE: `--apply` self-healing edits files with no undo until the repo is under git — keep it
diagnose-only until git is initialised.

## Secrets service — removed 2026-07-12
A Node/Express + MongoDB (Atlas M0) encrypted credential-store service (`secrets-service/`,
AES-256-GCM envelope encryption, bearer-token CRUD API) was built 2026-07 but never wired into
the n8n workflow. Removed once credential migration between PCs was solved a simpler way: n8n's
own `export:credentials`/`import:credentials` CLI plus its local encryption key (see
`SECOND-PC-SETUP.md` in the repo root) — no second always-on service to run, secure, or keep an
Atlas cluster alive for. Recreate from this history if a real multi-consumer secrets store is
ever needed again.

## Channel identity & monetization strategy (Nexiora)
The channel is branded **Nexiora** — a faceless daily **US-targeted tech/AI news + editorial**
channel (handle assumed `@Nexiora`; confirm/replace the URL in `Calculate Chapters` if different).
Brand palette: dark navy `#1a1a2e` + accent pink-red `#e94560` (matches thumbnail generator).

**Runs a US channel from India:** targeting is US (regionCode US, English, 5 PM ET publish, US
trending source) while the AdSense/payout account stays India-based (file W-8BEN US tax info once
monetized). No VPN needed. Set **Country of residence = United States** in YouTube Studio.

**Monetization (YPP, verified 2026):** full ad revenue needs **1,000 subs + 4,000 public
watch-hours/12mo** (Shorts-feed hours don't count); early access (memberships/Super Thanks) at
**500 subs + 3,000 hrs**. Long-form 8+ min enables multiple mid-rolls (~20x Shorts RPM). Q4
(Oct-Dec) gives ~1.6-2.1x RPM. US tech CPM ~$8-25; AI/SaaS/business/finance $15-90 (hence the
`cpmBoost`). Diversify beyond ads: **affiliate (AI/SaaS tools, 20-40% recurring)**, sponsorships,
memberships.

**CRITICAL RISK — inauthentic-content policy (renamed July 15 2025; mass terminations Jan 2026):**
YouTube demonetizes/terminates **mass-produced, templated, low-variation faceless output** — which
a naive daily auto-pipeline resembles. AI/faceless is NOT banned; templated slop is. Mitigations
applied/recommended: editorial-take script prompt, thumbnail variation, high-CPM topic bias, and
(recommended, not yet done) **reduce cadence to 3-4 higher-effort videos/week** + per-video charts +
enable YouTube "altered content" AI disclosure on upload.

